<title>BRAZIL: Brazil sugar crop max around 13.7 mln tns - DataNet.</title>
<headline>Brazil sugar crop max around 13.7 mln tns - DataNet.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's 1996/97 sugar crop could at best total around 13.7 million tonnes, tel quel, but could be as low as 13.15 million tonnes, according to independent consultants DataNet-Commodities.</p>
<p>&quot;The most optimistic scenario is for around 13.7 million tonnes, allowing for 10 million to 10.1 million tonnes in the center-south and 3.6 million to 3.7 million in the north/northeast,&quot; said analyst Aloisio Sotero.</p>
<p>&quot;However another scenario could see production of only 9.8 million tonnes in the center-south and 3.35 million in the north/northeast, giving a total of 13.15 million,&quot; he added.</p>
</text>
